Z||000007||Formula88||06-04-2001||10:27 PM||||They are shortened shifter levers. Since the shifter is cable actuated, it's throw doesn't change, but by shortening the lever arm, you get a shorter shifter.  Rodney Dickman also sells shifter that also have a longer lower lever arm to further shorten the throw, but his are $79.||||reg||1
Z||000008||sqoach||06-04-2001||11:34 PM||||These are shortened shifter arms. (I guess that's a better way to put it) They allow for shorter throws. They also feel better and look better in my opinion. The price is with shipping. I may have to bump it up to $40 though. So I guess that would be $35 plus s/h, cuz it was running me almost $5 for s/h. And you don't need a new boot. I just sent BBJ one because his was a little worn and the plastic retainer was broken. You will need to shorten the boot just a bit, though. Or just fold it down. And you can use your factory shift knob.||||reg||1
Z||000009||cadaver||06-05-2001||11:12 PM||||Mine are $35 with shipping. Shorten the boot? I have never shortened the boot. It just squishes down.||||reg||1
